# Shared CI setup/cache machinery (referenced by every job in workflows/).
/.github/actions/                   @EZArchy

# Dependency-audit gate. `/.github/` has no catch-all rule, so these are listed
# ahead of the PR that creates them rather than landing unowned. The allowlist
# is the one that matters: an entry SUPPRESSES a security finding, making it an
# un-gating surface structurally identical to `EXCLUDES` in coverage-config.ts.
/.github/dependabot.yml             @EZArchy
/scripts/audit-deps.ts              @EZArchy
/scripts/audit-allowlist.json       @EZArchy

# Architectural dependency boundaries. Owned for the same reason as the
# allowlist above: `scripts/` has no catch-all, and every rule here is a gate
# whose LOOSENING is invisible in a diff read casually — widening the worker
# allowlist or dropping the production-only scope on the package rule would
# each re-open a boundary without touching a test.
/scripts/check-boundaries.ts        @EZArchy

# Secret-scan config. Same class as the audit allowlist above and owned for the
# same reason: every `[[allowlists]]` entry SUPPRESSES a secret finding, so this
# file is an un-gating surface. The entries are deliberately RULE-scoped
# (`targetRules`) rather than a blanket `paths` rule over test files — a path
# blanket would silently stop the scan seeing a real PAT or private key
# committed inside a test. Widening one to a bare `paths` entry is exactly the
# edit that must not pass unread.
/.gitleaks.toml                     @EZArchy

# Test-runner + lint config that decides what runs and how strictly.
/biome.json                         @EZArchy
/bunfig.toml                        @EZArchy
/tsconfig.typecheck.json            @EZArchy
# The BASE tsconfigs. `tsconfig.typecheck.json` and `tsconfig.tests.json` both
# `extends` the root one, and that is where `strict` + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
# are actually declared (web's declares `strict` for the web leg) — so owning
# only the leaf configs left the real strictness dial unowned.
/tsconfig.json                      @EZArchy
